// ==== Routed experts in llama.cpp's IQ blocks (IQ1_S, IQ2_XXS, IQ2_S, IQ3_XXS, IQ3_S): GGUF imports' MoE ====
// `kapitsa import` keeps routed experts of these types as the GGUF stores them (src/gguf/import.cpp: no requantization);
// the loader moves their bits into this layout (Qwen35::load_iq_experts, src/model/qwen35_iq.cpp). A stacked matrix
// [E, N, K] (rows r = e N + n; K % 256 == 0) is one buffer of sections:
//   Q  at 0:  a uint2 per 32-value sub-block j of row r, at r K/32 + j (IQ1_S: a uint).
//             IQ2_XXS: the block's aux pair (4 grid index bytes; 4 x 7 sign bits and the 4-bit scale s in bits 28-31).
//             IQ2_S:   the 4 grid index low bytes, then the 4 sign bytes (8 stored signs per grid point).
//             IQ3_S, IQ3_XXS: the 8 grid index (low) bytes (grid points of 4 values).
//             IQ1_S:   the 4 grid index low bytes (grid points of 8 values).
//   X1 at x1: IQ2_S: a ushort per sub-block, qh (2 index high bits per grid point) | scales << 8 (4-bit scales of
//             values 0-15 and 16-31). IQ3_S: a uint per sub-block, its 32 sign bits. IQ3_XXS: a uint per sub-block,
//             4 x 7 sign bits and the 4-bit scale s in bits 28-31. IQ1_S: a ushort per sub-block, qh (3 index high bits
//             per grid point in bits 0-11, the 3-bit scale s in bits 12-14, the shift's sign in bit 15).
//   X2 at x2: IQ3_S: a byte per sub-block, qh (one index high bit per grid point).
//   X3 at x3: IQ3_S: a byte per two sub-blocks, their 4-bit scales (low nibble: the even sub-block).
//   D  at d:  a half per 256-value block (llama.cpp's d), at r K/256 + b.
// Values: IQ2_XXS / IQ2_S d (2s + 1) / 8 * grid * sign (magnitudes 8, 25, 43); IQ3_S d (2s + 1) * grid * sign (grid
// 1-15, odd); IQ3_XXS d (2s + 1) / 4 * grid * sign (grid 4-62, even); IQ1_S d (2s + 1) (g +- 1/8) = d / 8 (2s + 1)
// (8 g +- 1), g in {-1, 0, 1}. Bytes per 256 values: 50 (IQ1_S), 66, 82, 98 (IQ3_XXS), 110, as the GGUF stores them.
// The grid tables are adapted from ggml's iq2xxs_grid, iq2s_grid, iq3xxs_grid, iq3s_grid and iq1s_grid_gpu
// (ggml/src/ggml-common.h, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES).
//
// Three kernel families, as for the other expert formats (wfmt.metal), with the shared expert in its MLX 8-bit group-64
// form (the importer's) beside the routed IQ experts:
//  * one or a few token rows (decode, the small-batch verify): moei_gu_rows_* / moei_down_rows_* (MoeIqParams), the
//    per-row MoE of moeg_*_rows: fp32 FMAs on activations held in registers, the weights decoded as nh_x_iq2.metal
//    does (iq.h: a grid point's 8 magnitude bytes as fp16 subnormals, its signs spread into bit 15 / 31, one 8-byte
//    gather per 8 values; the scales folded in once per sub-block), d once per sub-block;
//  * the 8-row verify (moe8i_gu_* / moe8i_down_*): verify8.metal's moe8 passes (moe8_plan's tiles: every touched expert
//    once for all its rows, the shared expert as one more tile) with the IQ weights as MMA A operands;
//  * prefill (qrmi_gu_* / qrmi_dn_*): the qrm design (qmm_moe3.metal) on moe_bucket3's tiles.
// The MMA forms take the weights exactly: a value's magnitude times its sub-block's (2s + 1) is an integer of at most
// 62 * 31 = 1922, and the bits of the integer q < 2048 read as a half are q * 2^-24 (subnormal, then the first normal
// binade), so the A operand is that integer; d and the constant go into an fp32 epilogue per 256-value block (the
// fp32 MMA chain of a block, then acc += chain * d * 2^21 (IQ2) / 2^22 (IQ3_XXS) / 2^24 (IQ3_S)). IQ1_S's operands are
// the integers (2s + 1) (8 g +- 1) themselves (at most 135, exact halves), its epilogue d / 8. With the activations as
// halves this is the arithmetic of the other formats' MMA paths, without their weight rounding.
//
// A grid point's A pairs (fragment f, k-slots 2c, 2c + 1: values f and f + 4 of the point, as the X8 table and qmr's
// permuted X order want them) come from a word pair with the magnitude bytes in the order (m0, m1, m4, m5),
// (m2, m3, m6, m7): the permuted tables below (IQ3_S builds it from two 4-value grid words), and the signs spread as
// nh_x2_dec8 does but to that order (iq_pairs).

constant constexpr uint kIq2xxs = 1, kIq2s = 2, kIq3s = 3, kIq3xxs = 4, kIq1s = 5;  // FMT

